## Codebase Discoveries
The existing users/me request returns both the user GID and workspace GIDs. Project creation and refresh discover workspaces even with an explicit selection. Several workspaces require --workspace; task listing still visits all workspaces. Refresh identifies already configured projects by GID across URL forms and preserves custom aliases, old names, and existing URLs. It fetches all pages and validates collisions before saving or rendering. Refresh does not rewrite the file when it adds no aliases. Configuration writes follow symlinks, create a temporary file beside the target before credentials or API calls, preserve comments and permissions, sync, close, and rename. YAML merged mappings remain valid. Private creation validates privacy_setting and the permalink before saving. If saving fails after creation, stderr gives the URL and unsaved alias and directs manual registration instead of another creation request. The implicit GET retry regression is covered by a local server that closes the connection.

